# Reading notes. Before boot, the General board gets six notes (tools/fixtures/files/notes-general): one expired,
# which boot moves to General.old and then rewrites General without it; one to all and one to "Decimus all"; and three
# that reach readers by their level, not their name: one to imm and one to imp, both from Quintus, and one to 20
# (level 20 and up). The Ideas board gets one good note and then a bad keyword, which boot logs. In the temple (3001):
# Decimus (10), Quintus (25, who sees the level-20 note) and Smokegod (60, the top level, who sees all of them).
# Decimus reads, lists, changes board, catches up, reads past the last board and tries to remove; Smokegod removes.
# The board listing at login shows each player's unread notes. Last, a charmed fido is ordered to use note and board,
# which mobs can't.
@place notes-general ../notes/General
@place notes-bad ../notes/Ideas
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@file ../notes/General
@file ../notes/General.old
@connect quin
Quintus
psswrd
@return
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@as dec
scroll 0
board
note list
note list 1
note list x
note
note
note
note
note read 1
board general
note read 99
note read 0
note read 3
note read 1
note read again
note catchup
board 4
note catchup
note
note
board 99
board 0
board nothing
board announce
board 3
board 1
note remove
note remove x
note remove 99
note remove 1
note purge
note archive
note foo
@as quin
scroll 0
note list
note read 3
note
@as god
scroll 0
note list
note read 3
note read 4
note read 5
note remove 3
note list
@file ../notes/General
@as dec
note list
@mob 3062 3001
@charm
order fido note
@pulse 12
order fido board
@pulse 12
